Z||000000||Spyder||02-25-2000||12:02 PM||||My Fiero is running GREAT!<BR>What am I doing wrong?||||reg||1
Z||000001||ChadMan||02-25-2000||01:23 PM||||Start by unplugging your MAP sensor.  Then sand the insulation off two of your plug wires and twist-tie them together.  Next, crack your distributor with a mallet and dump a cup of water on it.  Finally, loosen your valve cover bolts so they leak plenty of oil, but don't ever add any oil to the engine.  That ought to fix you up!||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRH||02-25-2000||01:58 PM||||bahhahahaha... (sinister laughter)<P>Now that you put that in writing, EVERYTHING will go wrong!!!!<P>bahhahahaha||||reg||12
Z||000003||bHooper||02-25-2000||04:19 PM||||don't forget to unplug the relay on the right headlight and wind it to the up position!   you may also want losen the ground wire on the battery a bit... that way when you hit a bump, it'll make you think that something is wrong with the car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||02-25-2000||04:43 PM||||If your car is running great are you sure you didn't jump into the Honda by mistake.(Duck and cover, flame suit on- I'm ready)||||reg||1
Z||000005||Shiner||02-25-2000||05:11 PM||||Just wait a little while.  Before you know it, your little car will have smoked another crappy GM alternator (a high-wear item in any GM car.  Always carry a spare or two in the trunk)  Pretty soon, you will be coming home at night, drunk and crying, with a case of STP under your arm   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Shiner (edited 02-25-2000).]||||reg||12
